{%- comment %}
Task 20 (spec §F.5). Deliberately NOT layouts/base.liquid. base.liquid pulls
in the WebC CSS/JS bundles, preloaded webfonts, the nav rail + skip link,
the Atom/RSS <link> tags, rel=me, and the speedlify widget — none of which
belong inside a page a screenshot service photographs at 1200×630 (spec:
"base.liquid drags in site JS, WebC bundles, feeds, rel=me, Pagefind body
attr — none wanted inside a screenshot"). This layout is intentionally
minimal and self-contained: one dedicated stylesheet
(content/_css/opengraph.scss, compiled the same way every other .scss file
in this theme is — see _11ty/sassPlugin.js), no script, no navigation.

noindex is unconditional here (not the front-matter-driven `{% if noindex %}`
base.liquid uses) — every page built through this layout is a card, never a
page meant to be crawled or landed on directly.
{% endcomment -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8">
	<meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">
	<title>{{ site.name }} — social card</title>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="/_css/opengraph.css">
</head>
<body>{{ content }}</body>
</html>
